<div class="xsto-container py-8 md:py-12 mr-discovery"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Self-levelling wheelchairs, explained.","description":"Understand self-levelling wheelchair technology, explore the XSTO range and learn what to check during a personal demonstration.","inLanguage":"en-GB","dateModified":"2026-10-01","mainEntityOfPage":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/pages/self-levelling-wheelchairs","author":{"@id":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/#organization"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/#organization"}}</script><p class="mr-discovery-eyebrow">Understanding the technology</p><header class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Buyer guides","item":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/pages/guides"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Self-levelling wheelchairs, explained.","item":"https://mobilityrobot.co.uk/pages/self-levelling-wheelchairs"}]}</script><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-4 text-xs text-muted-foreground"><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><a href="/" class="hover:text-gold">Home</a></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/pages/guides" class="hover:text-gold">Buyer guides</a></li><li class="flex items-center gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page" class="font-medium text-foreground">Self-levelling wheelchairs, explained.</span></li></ol></nav><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-foreground md:text-4xl">Self-levelling wheelchairs, explained.</h1><p class="mt-3 text-lg text-muted-foreground">Understand self-levelling wheelchair technology, explore the XSTO range and learn what to check during a personal demonstration.</p></header><div class="mr-discovery-article-layout"><article class="mr-discovery-article" aria-label="Self-levelling wheelchairs, explained."><p class="mr-discovery-note">Updated <time dateTime="2026-10-01">1 October 2026</time> · Mobility Robot buying guidance</p><p>A self-levelling wheelchair adjusts its chassis or seating as the ground angle changes, within its operating limits. Self-levelling is different from seat lifting and does not, by itself, mean a wheelchair can climb stairs.</p><section aria-labelledby="what-is-self-levelling"><h2 id="what-is-self-levelling">What is a self-levelling wheelchair?</h2><p>A self-levelling powered wheelchair uses sensors and controlled movement to adjust its chassis or seating as the ground angle changes. In the XSTO range, this technology is intended to help keep the rider more level within the model’s operating limits.</p><p>It is useful to separate this feature from electric seat lifting. Levelling responds to the ground; seat lifting changes your seating height. A chair can offer both, but they serve different purposes.</p></section><section aria-labelledby="models-to-compare"><h2 id="models-to-compare">Which XSTO models should you compare?</h2><p>The M4 and M4B are the starting point for everyday self-levelling mobility. The M4B adds an improved folding footrest and new front suspension. The M4 Pro offers more seating adjustment. The X12 and X12 Pro add a separate stair-climbing capability.</p><p>Look at the complete chair as well as the levelling system. Seat height, user capacity, dimensions and controls all affect which model is practical for your day.</p><div class="mr-discovery-article-links"><a href="/pages/compare">Compare the five XSTO models <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></section><section aria-labelledby="operating-limits"><h2 id="operating-limits">What the feature does not tell you</h2><p>Self-levelling does not mean a chair can travel safely over any surface or climb any obstacle. Check its permitted gradients, dimensions, user capacity and manual. A maximum slope figure does not describe every real-world route.</p><p>Self-levelling and stair climbing are different capabilities. The M4, M4B and M4 Pro are not stair-climbing chairs. If stairs are part of your requirements, discuss the X12 and the suitability of the particular staircase with the team.</p><div class="mr-discovery-article-links"><a href="/pages/stair-climbing-wheelchairs">Read the stair-climbing buyer guide <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></section><section aria-labelledby="your-demonstration"><h2 id="your-demonstration">Make the demonstration about your day</h2><p>Bring a short list of the places you use regularly and the things you want to make easier. A personal demonstration is an opportunity to explore the details that a product video cannot answer for you.</p><ul><li>Try the controls and the response to stopping and turning.</li><li>Check the seat, backrest and footrest with your usual footwear and cushion requirements.</li><li>Measure the doors, lifts and storage spaces you use.</li><li>Discuss the surfaces and gradients along your usual routes.</li><li>Check how you would transport the chair and whether its component weights are manageable.</li></ul></section><section aria-labelledby="choose-the-whole-chair"><h2 id="choose-the-whole-chair">Choose around the whole chair</h2><p>The most impressive feature is only part of the decision. Seating, transfers, transport and dependable aftercare all matter. Use the model comparison to shortlist, then talk through your requirements with the UK team.</p><div class="mr-discovery-article-links"><a href="/pages/demo">Request your demonstration <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></section><p class="mr-discovery-note">Product information is based on the published XSTO range. Check the relevant product page and confirm current specifications and your chosen configuration with the team before ordering.</p></article><aside class="mr-discovery-sidebar"><nav aria-label="In this guide"><h2>In this guide</h2><ol><li><a href="#what-is-self-levelling">What is a self-levelling wheelchair?</a></li><li><a href="#models-to-compare">Which XSTO models should you compare?</a></li><li><a href="#operating-limits">What the feature does not tell you</a></li><li><a href="#your-demonstration">Make the demonstration about your day</a></li><li><a href="#choose-the-whole-chair">Choose around the whole chair</a></li></ol></nav><div class="mr-discovery-aside-cta"><h2>Find your next move.</h2><p>Talk through your requirements with our UK team.</p><a href="/pages/demo" class="mr-discovery-button">Book a demo <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a><a href="/pages/compare" class="mr-discovery-link">Compare models <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></div></aside></div><section class="mr-discovery-related" aria-labelledby="related-guides-heading"><p class="mr-discovery-eyebrow">Keep exploring</p><h2 id="related-guides-heading">Your next question, answered.</h2><div class="mr-discovery-grid mr-discovery-grid-two"><article class="mr-guide-card"><h3><a href="/pages/stair-climbing-wheelchairs">Stair-climbing wheelchairs. Start with the right questions.</a></h3><p>The questions to ask about stairs, training and your everyday routes.</p><a href="/pages/stair-climbing-wheelchairs" class="mr-discovery-link">Read the guide <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></article><article class="mr-guide-card"><h3><a href="/pages/choosing-an-xsto-wheelchair">Which XSTO is right for you?</a></h3><p>A practical way to compare the M4, M4B, M4 Pro, X12 and X12 Pro around your own life.</p><a href="/pages/choosing-an-xsto-wheelchair" class="mr-discovery-link">Read the guide <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10" /> <path d="M7 17 17 7" /></svg></a></article></div></section></div>
